{% doc %}
won-site-schema — emit a site-level WebSite JSON-LD node with a SearchAction, so
search + AI engines understand the store as a whole and know its search entry
point (the machine-readable "store map" a theme CAN ship). Complements — does not
duplicate — the base theme's Organization node.

Wired into the layout <head> by compose (step 2b) and self-limited to the
homepage, so exactly one WebSite node is emitted per store.

NOTE: a canonical `/llms.txt` file is NOT a theme route (Shopify only lets themes
customise robots.txt, and won-base ships code, not templates). Serving a real
`/llms.txt` store map is an app / app-proxy / hosting concern — see the Won Toasts
/ app layer (Fáze 8). This snippet is the theme-native equivalent.
@example
{% render 'won-site-schema' %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- if request.page_type == 'index' -%}
  {%- assign won_site_url = shop.url -%}
  {%- capture won_site_json -%}{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebSite","name":{{ shop.name | json }},"url":{{ won_site_url | json }},"potentialAction":{"@type":"SearchAction","target":{"@type":"EntryPoint","urlTemplate":{{ won_site_url | append: '/search?q={search_term_string}' | json }}},"query-input":"required name=search_term_string"}}{%- endcapture -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">{{ won_site_json | replace: '</', '<\/' }}</script>
{%- endif -%}
